  "lineage": "Classic soul is a retrospective discovery and listening category for established soul repertoire, overlapping regional Memphis, Southern, Motown and other soul traditions. The source-author roster explicitly includes Al Green alongside Marvin Gaye, Aretha Franklin and Otis Redding. This representative Al Green/Hi branch takes the documented singer, organ, guitar, bass, drum and conga interplay of Let’s Stay Together as a starting point. The authored reduction includes vocal support but omits the recording’s horn and string layers; it does not invent an exclusive classic-soul instrument set or equate the entire category with one Memphis session.",
